Time to build your monster's **Mood & Status Beacon**!

### Breadboard Wiring Mission:
1. Insert your Common Cathode RGB LED across separate rows on the breadboard.
2. Connect the **longest pin (Pin 2)** directly to Arduino **GND**.
3. Connect **Pin 1 (Red)** through a **220Ω resistor** to Uno **PWM Pin ~9**.
4. Connect **Pin 3 (Green)** through a **220Ω resistor** to Uno **PWM Pin ~10**.
5. Connect **Pin 4 (Blue)** through a **220Ω resistor** to Uno **PWM Pin ~11**.

### The Status Light Sketch:
```cpp
const int RED_PIN = 9;    // PWM Pin ~9
const int GREEN_PIN = 10; // PWM Pin ~10
const int BLUE_PIN = 11;  // PWM Pin ~11

void setup() {
  pinMode(RED_PIN, OUTPUT);
  pinMode(GREEN_PIN, OUTPUT);
  pinMode(BLUE_PIN, OUTPUT);
}

void setColor(int red, int green, int blue) {
  analogWrite(RED_PIN, red);
  analogWrite(GREEN_PIN, green);
  analogWrite(BLUE_PIN, blue);
}

void loop() {
  // 🟢 Green = Ready / Systems Clear
  setColor(0, 255, 0);
  delay(1500);

  // 🟡 Yellow = Warning / Charging
  setColor(255, 180, 0);
  delay(1500);

  // 🔴 Red = Alert / Stop!
  setColor(255, 0, 0);
  delay(1500);

  // 🟣 Purple = Party Mode Beacon!
  setColor(200, 0, 255);
  delay(1500);
}
```

Upload this sketch to watch your monster express its status in living color!
